  "limitations": [
    "Measures incremental native policy and reclamation cost under a common synthetic producer; not total semantic-estimator cost.",
    "No automatic semantic deletion, model judge, R-KV redundancy estimator, DSH quality, block-graph workload or tail-latency qualification.",
    "One synthetic publication of four candidate blocks per measured DELETE request; not a saturation or long-session benchmark.",
    "All paired outputs agree while the active GPU window remains stable; this does not prove quality after later retrieval omits deleted content.",
    "Request-lifecycle CPU release counts include cleanup. Only candidate_counts_during_decode and release_witnesses prove in-decode GC.",
    "Five-pair bootstrap is descriptive and workload-specific; passing a 1% margin is not a proof of zero overhead.",
    "Nonfatal allocator OOM retries occur during NVFP4 loading; engines subsequently start and complete. Shutdown emits EngineDeadError after intentional SIGTERM and a semaphore cleanup warning.",
    "Terminal M may be deferred after deleted history still exists in the GPU window; this run does not qualify successful M restoration after GC.",
    "OFF captures terminal M (3.29-3.49 ms host time); DELETE defers M and rewinds to P224. Net throughput includes this terminal-path difference and excludes next-turn replay cost."
  ],
